---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About Kalorec</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    Kalorec is a recipe manager that stores your recipes as plain JSON files in a GitHub repo you choose — not a database you don't control. Add recipes by hand or import them from a link, tag and search them, and edit them like any other file in your repo.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    Your source recipes live in a private GitHub repo you choose, so they stay portable and versioned. To share one, Kalorec copies that recipe into a separate public sharing repo for your profile. Visitors read only those published copies and can view or copy them.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    Unpublishing removes the current public copy, but GitHub history and copies made while it was public can persist. If you previously stored recipes in a public source repo, those files may remain exposed in its history even after moving to private source storage.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    New here? See <a href="/how-to-use" class="text-green-700 dark:text-green-400">How to Use</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
